<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 3 December, from 915 to 1984.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">915 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope John X crowns Berengar I of Italy as emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At St Peter's Basilica in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, Pope John X crowned Berengar I, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, as emperor, after Berengar had supplied troops for the campaign against the Saracens. Berengar in turn confirmed earlier emperors' donations to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy">Berengar I of Italy</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperator-romanorum">Imperator Romanorum</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1283">1283 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">743 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongol forces take the Burmese fort at Ngasaunggyan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After withstanding a Mongol siege for over two months, the Burmese fort at Ngasaunggyan fell to the invading forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>. The invasions eventually toppled the 250-year-old Pagan Empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-mongol-invasion-of-burma">First Mongol invasion of Burma</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1552">1552 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">474 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francis Xavier dies within sight of China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-xavier">Francis Xavier</a> died of fever on Shangchuan Island while waiting to enter mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. He had preached in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, and was canonised in 1622.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Paul Jones hoists the Continental Union Flag on the Alfred</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a>, Lieutenant John Paul Jones hoisted the Continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-flag">Union Flag</a> aboard the Alfred, a frigate of the Continental Navy, the first vessel to fly the flag. It remained the de facto flag of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> until 1777.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1800">1800 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Moreau defeats the Austrians at Hohenlinden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French forces under General Jean Moreau crushed an Austrian army in snowy forest east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>. The defeat forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> to make peace at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneville">Lunéville</a> in February 1801.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1910">1910 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">116 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Georges Claude shows neon lighting at the Paris Motor Show</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> Motor Show, the French engineer Georges Claude displayed glowing tubes of neon gas. Neon signs soon became a fixture of advertising and city nightlife worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christiaan Barnard performs the first human heart transplant</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Groote Schuur Hospital in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a>, Christiaan Barnard's team transplanted a heart into Louis Washkansky. He lived for 18 days before dying of pneumonia, but the operation launched transplant surgery.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1984">1984 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">42 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Toxic gas leaks from a pesticide plant in Bhopal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Methyl isocyanate escaped from a Union Carbide plant in Bhopal overnight, killing thousands within days. Total deaths are estimated in the range of 15,000 or more, and hundreds of thousands suffered lasting harm.</p></div></li></ol>
